    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d419">

                <pb facs="0404" n="396" sameAs="frus:frus1939v05/pg396"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.5151/1392: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-05-27T13:00:00-03:00">May 27, 1939—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 27—11:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>179. A list of American arrears is proceeding satisfactorily and the Director of
                    Exchange informs me that all American arrears not covered by exchange contracts
                    will be paid in full before the middle of June.</p>
                <pb facs="0405" n="397" xml:id="pg397"/>
                <p>The Bank of Brazil has instructed its agency in Bahia to suspend the purchase of
                    German compensation marks in payment for cocoa for exportation to Germany. This
                    decision was made after the bank received notice that German firms had
                    contracted for 240,000 bags of Bahia cocoa. (Director of Exchange suspects that
                    the German firms intend to dispose of most of this cocoa in other
                    countries.)</p>
                <p>Please inform Department of Commerce.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
